# MSP Chargeback prototype

A shareable prototype published to GitHub Pages at https://ddrlacic.github.io/msp-chargeback/. Pushing to `main` deploys it.

## Sources of truth

- **Technology: `../msp-ui`** (Angular 21, zoneless, signals, Tailwind v4, Lucide, Vitest). Follow its rules in `../msp-ui/.cursor/rules/` for code structure, naming and testing.
- **UI: `../menu-app`** (Management Center). Match its look and behaviour. Look in `../menu-app/frontend-migration/libs/admin-ui` for components and `../menu-app/frontend-migration/libs/admin-ui/src/assets/styles/scss/_01-settings` for tokens. Copy for labels and messages follows `../menu-app/docs/design/ux-copy-principles.md`.
- Chargeback behaviour and field names: `../msp-ui/src/app/features/home/chargebacks` and `../msp-ui/src/app/services`.
- Requirements and Worldpay research: `docs/` (git-ignored, local only; start with `docs/README.md`). Never commit it or copy its content into the app.

## Build phases and UI skills

- Build in the phases from `docs/prototype-plan.md`, one phase per chat.
- UI skills are linked in `.claude/skills/`: `better-ui`, `better-typography`, `better-colors`, `emil-design-eng`, `find-animation-opportunities`. Read the relevant one before UI or motion work.

## Dev handoff spec

- `docs/handoff/` is the build spec for msp-ui developers and their AI agents. Start at `docs/handoff/README.md`.
- Write the handoff docs for a page only once the user says they're satisfied with its design. While the design is still changing, change only the prototype; don't touch `docs/handoff/` until then.
- When the user approves a page, update every matching handoff file in that session: status model, screen, component, data, copy, acceptance criteria.
- At that point, new decisions go to `docs/handoff/decisions.md` and unresolved ones to `docs/handoff/open-questions.md`. Record only the final design, not the options that were tried and dropped.

## This repo is public

- Re-create behaviour and wording; never copy source files, internal docs, credentials, API URLs, or real merchant, cardholder or chargeback data from msp-ui or menu-app.
- All data is fake and lives in the prototype.

## Code rules

- No comments of any kind.
- Angular CLI only: `ng serve`, `ng test`, `ng build`. Never `npm run` or `vitest run`.
- `input()`, `output()`, `computed()`, `signal()`, `inject()`; `@if`, `@for`, `@switch`; host bindings in `host: {}`.
- Standalone components with `ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`.
- Tailwind utility classes and the tokens in `src/styles.scss`; no hardcoded colours in components; Lucide icons only; component SCSS stays empty.
- Tests: `toBe()` and `toEqual()`, `toHaveBeenCalledOnce()`; no `toBeTruthy()` or `toBeDefined()`; no `as any`.
- Routing uses hash location so shared links work on GitHub Pages. Keep it.
- No backend: data comes from typed fixtures and signal-based services.

## Working agreement

- The user verifies in the browser. Do not open the prototype yourself; list what changed and what to check.
- Local server: `ng serve`, then `http://localhost:4200/`.
- Current msp-ui for reference: `ng serve` in `../msp-ui`, then `http://localhost:8080/`. Its `src/environment.js` points to the dev API locally and is marked `skip-worktree`, so it's never committed.
